# Serverless Functions: Vercel vs Supabase Edge

## Decision Guide

**Choose the right serverless platform based on your use case:**

| Use Case | Platform | Why |
|----------|----------|-----|
| App request/response flow | Vercel | Tight Next.js integration |
| Complex business logic | Vercel | Full Node.js + npm ecosystem |
| Form handling & mutations | Vercel | Server Actions support |
| Database triggers | Supabase Edge | Direct DB event access |
| Scheduled jobs (cron) | Supabase Edge | Built-in scheduling |
| External webhooks | Supabase Edge | Decoupled from app |
| Ultra-low latency globally | Supabase Edge | Edge runtime worldwide |


## Rule of Thumb

- **Part of app's request/response flow** → Vercel (Next.js API routes)
- **Reacting to events** (DB changes, webhooks, cron) → Supabase Edge
- **Need Node.js packages** → Vercel
- **Need ultra-low latency globally** → Supabase Edge


## Platform Comparison

### Vercel (Next.js API Routes)

**Location:** `src/app/api/`

**Runtime:** Node.js

**Best for:**
- OCR processing, AI/ML calls (like our `/api/ocr`)
- Session management tied to the app (like our `/api/sessions`)
- Authenticated endpoints using Next.js middleware
- Anything needing npm packages

**Refer to:** `api-routes.mdc` for implementation patterns


### Supabase Edge Functions

**Location:** `supabase/functions/`

**Runtime:** Deno (not Node.js)

**Best for:**
- Webhook receivers (Stripe, GitHub, etc.)
- Scheduled cleanup tasks
- Database-triggered actions
- Standalone microservices

**Refer to:** `supabase-functions.mdc` for implementation patterns


## Current Project Usage

| Route | Platform | Purpose |
